{{!
    @template enrol_apply/review_rules

    "Rules to observe": one meter per limit a confirmation touches, then the deferred count and
    the earlier applications. Rendered only when one of them is present.

    Each meter's bar is decoration (aria-hidden): the seats already taken striped, the
    applicant's own solid, coloured by the occupancy AFTER confirming. The line under it says the
    same thing in words and is what a screen reader reads. One meter per line, so a label and
    its count never wrap together.

    "See the history" opens a dialogue, so it is a button: enrol_apply/review moves the server's
    own list (enrol_apply/review_history) into a core/modal. Without JavaScript the button is
    hidden and the list is shown in place below.

    Context variables required for this template:
    * hasrules boolean - whether there is anything to show
    * rulesheading string - the section's heading
    * hasmeters boolean, meters array - one entry per limit, each with:
      * label string - what the limit is, plain spelling
      * isgroup, isplaces, isapplicants boolean - which limit, which picks the icon
      * count string - how many it holds now, "18 of 20"
      * takenpercent int, ownpercent int - the striped and the solid part of the bar
      * barclass string - the level's background and text colour classes, a literal pair
      * isdanger boolean - whether the level is danger, which weights the line
      * after string - what confirming leaves, plain spelling
    * hasdeferredline boolean, deferredline string - how many deferred applications hold room
    * hashistoryline boolean, historyline string - the earlier applications, counted, the last named
    * historyopen string - the button's label

    Example context (json):
    {
        "hasrules": true,
        "rulesheading": "Rules to observe",
        "hasmeters": true,
        "meters": [
            {
                "label": "Turma A (key group)", "isgroup": true, "count": "18 of 20", "takenpercent": 90,
                "ownpercent": 5, "barclass": "bg-danger text-white", "isdanger": true,
                "after": "On confirming: 19 of 20, 1 left"
            },
            {
                "label": "Places on this method", "isplaces": true, "count": "33 of 50", "takenpercent": 66,
                "ownpercent": 2, "barclass": "bg-warning text-dark", "after": "On confirming: 34 of 50, 16 left"
            }
        ],
        "hasdeferredline": true,
        "deferredline": "2 deferred applications count against the limit of 60 applications",
        "hashistoryline": true,
        "historyline": "2 earlier applications to this course. The last: Cancelled, 12/03/26, 09:14.",
        "historyopen": "See the history"
    }
}}
{{#hasrules}}
<section class="enrol_apply-rules enrol_apply-box" aria-labelledby="enrol_apply_rules_heading">
    <h2 class="enrol_apply-blocktitle" id="enrol_apply_rules_heading">{{rulesheading}}</h2>
    {{#hasmeters}}
        <ul class="enrol_apply-meters list-unstyled mb-0">
            {{#meters}}
                <li class="enrol_apply-reviewmeter">
                    <div class="enrol_apply-meterhead">
                        <span>{{#isgroup}}{{#pix}}i/group, core{{/pix}}{{/isgroup}}{{#isplaces}}{{#pix}}i/enrolusers, core{{/pix}}{{/isplaces}}{{#isapplicants}}{{#pix}}i/users, core{{/pix}}{{/isapplicants}}{{label}}</span>
                        <span class="enrol_apply-metercount">{{count}}</span>
                    </div>
                    <div class="progress enrol_apply-meterbar" aria-hidden="true">
                        <div class="progress-bar progress-bar-striped {{barclass}}" style="width: {{takenpercent}}%"></div>
                        <div class="progress-bar {{barclass}}" style="width: {{ownpercent}}%"></div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="enrol_apply-meterafter{{#isdanger}} enrol_apply-meterafter-danger{{/isdanger}}" data-region="meter-after">{{after}}</div>
                </li>
            {{/meters}}
        </ul>
    {{/hasmeters}}
    {{#hasdeferredline}}
        <p class="enrol_apply-rulefact" data-region="rules-deferred">{{#pix}}i/duration, core{{/pix}}<span>{{deferredline}}</span></p>
    {{/hasdeferredline}}
    {{#hashistoryline}}
        <p class="enrol_apply-rulefact" data-region="rules-history">{{#pix}}e/restore_last_draft, core{{/pix}}<span>{{historyline}} <button type="button" class="btn btn-link p-0 align-baseline enrol_apply-historybutton" data-action="enrol_apply-history" aria-haspopup="dialog">{{historyopen}}</button></span></p>
    {{/hashistoryline}}
</section>
{{/hasrules}}
